<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Pour</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>pour &lt;container&gt; into &lt;container&gt;
pour &lt;container&gt; out
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>pour fountain into waterskin
pour barrel into cup
pour cup out
</pre>
<p>Pours a drink from one container into another: to fill your waterskin at 
a fountain, say. It pours as much as the second container holds. Both 
must be drink containers, and you can't pour one drink into another: the 
second container must be empty, or hold the same drink.
</p><p>Beware: poison goes with the drink. If the first container is poisoned, 
what you pour into the second is too.
</p><p>To empty a container you carry, pour it out. Some, such as a fountain, can 
never be emptied.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Drink</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Taste</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Sip</a>
</pre>




</div>